# Supervisor mode takes a nested supervisor software interrupt after re-enabling SIE.
# Host setup preloads:
# - privilege = Supervisor
# - controller source 1 enabled, routed to supervisor, and pending
# - mideleg/sie enable supervisor external and software interrupts
# - sstatus.SIE enabled
# - stvec = 0x20 in vectored mode
# The outer supervisor-external handler saves sepc/sstatus, claims and completes
# the controller source, records x10 = 10, re-enables SIE, raises SSIP through
# MMIO, then resumes after the nested handler to record x11 = 11, restore state,
# and sret. The inner supervisor-software handler clears SSIP, records x12 = 12,
# and sret returns to the outer handler. Mainline finally resumes and writes x1 = 1.
# Expect x1 = 1, x10 = 10, x11 = 11, x12 = 12, x21 = 21, privilege = Supervisor.
